map()

map() runs a function on every item in an array and returns a new array.

Example: double every number.

const numbers = [1, 2, 3, 4];
const doubledNumbers = numbers.map(number => number * 2);
console.log(doubledNumbers);

Output:
[2, 4, 6, 8]

Example: convert names to uppercase.

const students = ["priynshu", "riya", "aman"];
const upperCaseNames = students.map(name => name.toUpperCase());
console.log(upperCaseNames);

["PRIYANSHU", "RIYA", "AMAN"]